Fast-paced punch exchange — @image2 attacks at full speed in a relentless combo, @image1 matches the speed perfectly to counter every strike, creating a rapid back-and-forth exchange, but every counter from @image1 is a deflection/parry, never a damaging blow.
@image2 explodes forward with a blazing-fast six-hit combo — jab, cross, claw-slash, hook, knee, claw-uppercut — each strike carrying full smear-frame motion blur and sharp recoil between hits. @image1 matches the speed exactly, his arms moving in fast, fluid counter-motions: parrying the jab with a wrist flick, redirecting the cross with a forearm block, sidestepping the claw-slash with a sharp pivot, catching the hook on his palm, sweeping the knee aside with his shin, and finally stopping the claw-uppercut dead with two fingers — each parry releasing a small shockwave-spark of wind at the point of contact, fabric and hair snapping with every fast motion. The entire exchange should feel like a true high-speed trade of blows, both fighters moving in perfect synchronized tempo, but the outcome makes it clear: every single one of @image2's attacks fails completely, while @image1 expends almost no force. @image2 skids back half a step after the final parry, breathing hard, eyes burning with frustration. @image1 stands exactly where he started, posture completely relaxed, not even breathing heavier. @image2 snarls: 「なぜ効かない!」[JP | Naze kikanai! | EN: "Why isn't it working!?"]
Camera: rapid alternating whip-pans synced to each of the six strikes (one whip-pan per hit), motion blur intensity high throughout the exchange, slowing into a smooth settle-shot on @image2 skidding back, ending on a static close-up with subtle breathing sway for the dialogue line.16:9.
